<title>USA: U.S. Ex-Im Bank backs $135 mln sale to Gazprom.</title>
<headline>U.S. Ex-Im Bank backs $135 mln sale to Gazprom.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Export-Import Bank approved a $134.6 million loan guarantee backing a sale of natural gas compressors to Russia's Gazprom from Iowa-based Compressor Controls Corp.</p>
<p>The deal was the first approved under a 1994 memorandum of understanding between Ex-Im Bank and Gazprom, the world's largest natural gas company.</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan Bank NA Inc is the guaranteed lender.</p>
<p>The loan is due to be repaid in five tranches, beginning in July 1998, Ex-Im Bank said.</p>
</text>
